The intersection of the two arcs forms an isosceles triangle $AEC$ with $AE = EC = 4$ cm.
The area of this triangle can be calculated using the formula $A = \frac{1}{2}ab\sin(C)$, where $a$ and $b$ are sides of the triangle and $C$ is the included angle.
In this case, $a = b = 4$ cm and $C = 90^\circ$.
So the area of triangle $AEC$ is $A = \frac{1}{2}(4)(4)\sin(90^\circ) = 8$ cm$^2$.
The area of each circle is $\pi r^2 = \pi(4)^2 = 16\pi$ cm$^2$.
So the total area of the football-shaped region is $2(16\pi) - 8 = 32\pi - 8$ cm$^2$.
