The area of a quadrilateral can be calculated using the shoelace formula: 

$$Area = \frac{1}{2} \left| \sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (x_i y_{i+1} - x_{i+1} y_i) + (x_1 y_n - x_n y_1) \right|$$

However, this formula is inherently 2-dimensional. Since the flat quadrilateral is in 3D space, we'll need to break down the area into two triangular regions using the midpoints of the non-parallel sides.

